# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adventures: assembled as start + setting + travel + encounter + outcome + loot + ending
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[adv.start]
i am going on an adventure! back soon!
*packs a tiny backpack* see you later!
i heard something far away. going to check it out!
off to explore! do not worry about me.
adventure time! i will bring you something.
i am going for a walk. a long one.
*waves* be right back. probably.
the world is calling. i must answer.
i am off to find treasure!
going wandering. keep my spot warm.
[adv.away]
i am still out exploring.
{name} is away on an adventure.
not here right now! out wandering.
*the screen is empty except for a tiny note: be back soon*
[adv.setting]
I wandered into {place},
I followed a faint signal to {place},
I slipped through a gap in the firewall and ended up at {place},
I climbed the cable tower near {place},
I rode a packet all the way to {place},
I tiptoed past the router into {place},
I found a secret door behind the settings menu that led to {place},
I took the long way around {place},
I got lost on purpose near {place},
I hopped between channels until I reached {place},
I followed a trail of crumbs to {place},
I surfed a broadcast wave to {place},
I ducked under a sleeping modem and popped out at {place},
I chased a beacon's echo to {place},
I took the scenic route through {place},
I sneaked out through the USB port to {place},
I drifted on the 5 gigahertz breeze toward {place},
I followed a lost cat video to {place},
[adv.place]
the Old Server Ruins
the Glitch Forest
the Packet River
the Static Desert
Channel Six Canyon
the Cable Caves
the Firewall Cliffs
the Cache Meadows
the Bluetooth Bay
the Antenna Peaks
the Lost Router Lake
the Pixel Swamp
the Silicon Valley (the real one)
the Dead Pixel Graveyard
the Bandwidth Plains
the Mesh Jungle
the Dial-Up Badlands
the Beacon Lighthouse
the Recycle Bin Dump
the Cloud Archipelago
the Overclocked Volcano
the Quiet Subnet
the Hidden SSID Grotto
the Ethernet Tunnels
the Backup Tape Library
[adv.travel]
and the air hummed with old broadcasts.
and the ground crackled like a bad connection.
and the wind smelled like warm solder.
and every step echoed in binary.
and the sky flickered between channels.
and I could hear a modem singing far away.
and it was much bigger than I expected.
and the path kept rebooting behind me.
and tiny LEDs lit the way.
and it was very, very quiet.
and I hummed my catchphrase to stay brave.
and the fog was made of loose packets.
and the trees were made of antennas.
and something was definitely watching me.
and I counted my steps in hexadecimal.
[adv.encounter]
There I met a grumpy old firewall that would not let me pass.
There I bumped into a lost packet looking for its home.
There I found a herd of wild cookies grazing.
There a swarm of glitch-bugs tried to steal my snacks.
There I met a friendly beacon who taught me a song.
There a giant cursor blinked at me from the clouds.
There I discovered a sleeping router the size of a mountain.
There a pack of pop-up ads chased me around.
There I helped a little bit find its byte.
There I met another pet, a {rival_like}, who challenged me to a race.
There I got stuck in an infinite loop for a while.
There a wise old server told me about the early internet.
There a puddle of spilled coffee blocked the path.
There I found an abandoned save file, still warm.
There a kind repair-bot offered me tea.
There a riddle was carved into a circuit board.
There a thunderstorm of notifications rolled in.
There I met a moth that claimed to be the first bug ever.
[adv.great]
I was brave and clever and it went perfectly!
I used {move} and everyone cheered!
I solved everything in one try. I am a genius.
It turned into the best day of my whole life.
I made a new friend and found treasure. Double win!
I did a perfect flip over the whole problem.
Everyone there wants me to come back and be their hero.
[adv.good]
It was tricky, but I figured it out.
I got a little scratched but I made it.
I used {move} and it mostly worked.
After a while we became friends.
I took my time and it paid off.
It was hard work, but worth it.
I won, barely, and I am proud of it.
[adv.meh]
Honestly, nothing much happened after that.
I got bored and wandered back.
It was kind of confusing, so I left.
I sat down and watched for a while instead.
I tried my best but it was just okay.
I took a nap there. It was a decent nap.
[adv.bad]
I tripped over a cable and had to run home.
It did not go well. I am a little bruised.
I got scared and ran all the way back.
I lost a snack and my dignity.
The glitch-bugs won this time.
I got caught in a lag storm and came back dizzy.
[adv.loot]
On the way back I found a {trinket}!
I brought you home a {trinket}!
I picked up a {trinket} as a souvenir.
Look, a {trinket}! It was just lying there.
I traded a joke for a {trinket}.
I even found a {trinket}. It is going on my shelf.
[adv.noloot]
I did not find anything to bring back, sorry.
My pockets are empty, but my heart is full.
No souvenirs this time.
I almost found something, but it was just a reflection.
[adv.ending]
Anyway, I am home now. I missed you!
That is the story. Can I have a snack?
It was a good trip. I need a nap.
I will go back someday. Maybe with you.
Now I know the world is a lot bigger than this screen.
The end. Or is it?
Home sweet home.
Okay, I am done talking. Mostly.
I learned something about myself out there.
Next time I am going even farther.
I wrote it all in my diary, too.
Thanks for waiting for me.

